      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To determine the value of \\( b + m \\) given the intersection point \\((6, 10)\\), we start by substituting \\(x = 6\\) and \\(y = 10\\) into the equations of the lines.\n\nFirst, substitute \\(x = 6\\) and \\(y = 10\\) into the equation \\(y = mx + 4\\):\n\n\\[\n10 = m \\cdot 6 + 4\n\\]\n\\[\n10 = 6m + 4\n\\]\n\\[\n10 - 4 = 6m\n\\]\n\\[\n6 = 6m\n\\]\n\\[\nm = 1\n\\]\n\nNext, substitute \\(x = 6\\) and \\(y = 10\\) into the equation \\(y = 3x + b\\):\n\n\\[\n10 = 3 \\cdot 6 + b\n\\]\n\\[\n10 = 18 + b\n\\]\n\\[\n10 - 18 = b\n\\]\n\\[\nb = -8\n\\]\n\nNow, find \\( b + m \\):\n\n\\[\nb + m = -8 + 1 = -7\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( b + m \\) is \\(\\boxed{-7}\\).",
