      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "The given equations are $y = mx + 4$ and $y = 3x + b$. Substituting the coordinates $(6, 10)$ into each equation to find $m$ and $b$, we get:\nFor the first equation:\n$$\n\\begin{align*}\n10 &= 6m + 4 \\\\\n16 &= 6m \\\\\nm &= \\frac{16}{6} = \\frac{8}{3}\n\\end{align*}\n$$\nFor the second equation:\n$$\n\\begin{align*}\n10 &= 3(6) + b \\\\\n10 &= 18 + b \\\\\nb &= 10 - 18 \\\\\nb &= -8\n\\end{align*}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have $b = -8$ and $m = \\frac{8}{3}$ for the equations. When we add these together, we get:\n$$\nb + m = -8 + \\frac{8}{3}\n$$\nTo add the fractions, we need a common denominator, which is 3:\n$$\nb + m = \\frac{-8}{1} + \\frac{8}{3} = \\frac{-24}{3} + \\frac{8}{3} = \\frac{-16}{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $\\boxed{-\\frac{16}{3}}$.",
